&lt;!-- It could be argued that linking the Pleiades entry for Vienne is helpful here, as it is the closest location available for this garden. --&gt;</description></item><item><title>Maison Au Nord De La Place Des Capucins</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/cd4e9b17fe/</link><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/cd4e9b17fe/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="dates"&gt;Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 1748 CE, north of the Place des Capucins, L. Charvet found ruins of a building within the Roman city walls. Later, in 1778 CE, several mosaics were discovered in the vincinity confirming the precense of one or more dwelings featuring high-quality ornamentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- For now, include dates exactly as written in the document. We will revisit the question of date formatting once more data have been collected. If no date, use "unspecified" --&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1748 CE, and again in 1778 CE.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- format as YYYY, or YYYY-YYYY --&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 1748, north of Place des Capucins, inside the ancient roman walls, ruins of a building were found that L. Charvet describes as ancient baths, which, from his description and without a known or surviving plan, appears to be the remains of a peristyle domus. A rectangular basin measuring 11 by 3 meters featured exedrae extending from three of its sides: it adorned a peristyle with 4-meter-wide porticoes, lined with columns of violet marble. Access to the garden is through two-stepped stairs situated in front of the porticoe. In 1778, multiple mosaics were found in the surrounding environment that confirmed the precense of one or more dwellings featuring high-quality decor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the excavation, traces of a violent fire on the walls of the basin and among the unearthed remains (mosaic fragments, charcoal, scorched stones, molten lead) were found. However, no dating of the site is given.&lt;/p&gt;
